==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|canonnade|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|eɪd}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Firing [[artillery]] in a large amount for a length of time .
#* Prescott
#*: A furious '''cannonade''' was kept up from the whole circle of batteries on the devoted town.
# {{figurative}} A loud noise like a cannonade; a [[boom]]ing.
#* Ewerson
#*: Blue Walden rolls its '''cannonade'''.

